*.pyc

# Runtime data written by the api-server (waitlist signups, job result
# cache) -- these are generated on first run, not source.
#
# cache.ts resolves DATA_DIR as `../data` relative to its own compiled
# location, which is `dist/` when running the built bundle (`pnpm dev`
# builds to dist/index.mjs and runs that) -- so the real runtime path is
# artifacts/api-server/data/, not src/data/. The old pattern below only
# matched a location the app never actually writes to when run the normal
# way, so a real cache.json (BRENDA/KEGG-resolved simulation results, not
# source) could slip past `git status` looking clean and get swept in by
# `git add -A`. Ignoring both locations since either can exist depending on
# how the server was started (built bundle vs. a future direct-from-src
# runner).
artifacts/api-server/data/*.json
artifacts/api-server/src/data/*.json
